{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 14,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.049,
            0.432,
            0.067
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.087,
            0.846,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 11:** Riyaz created a math trick, which he tries out on his friend Akash."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.132,
            0.847,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": "Riyaz asked Akash to perform the following steps without revealing the answer to any of the intermediate steps."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.176,
            0.38,
            0.195
          ],
          "content": "1. Think of a number."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.2,
            0.468,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": "2. Subtract 3 from the number."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.226,
            0.425,
            0.246
          ],
          "content": "3. Multiply the result by 4."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.251,
            0.399,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": "4. Add 8 to the product."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.275,
            0.425,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": "5. Reveal the final answer."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.3,
            0.626,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": "The final answer revealed by Akash was 24. Using this, Riyaz correctly figured out the starting number that Akash had thought of. Find this number."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.649,
            0.175,
            0.938,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.382,
            0.624,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": "Try the steps using different numbers as the"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.4,
            0.847,
            0.44
          ],
          "continues_prev": true,
          "content": "starting number. Do you see any relation between the starting number and final answer?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.445,
            0.847,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "The answer can be found by algebraically modeling this scenario. In other words, we can form an equation using an unknown. Let the unknown starting number be x."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.513,
            0.628,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": "What are the expressions we get after each step?"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.543,
            0.843,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": "| Steps | Expression |\n| --- | --- |\n| Think of a number. | x |\n| Subtract 3 from the number. | x - 3 |\n| Multiply the result by 4. | 4 (x - 3) = 4x - 12 |\n| Add 8 to the product. | 4x - 12 + 8 = 4x - 4 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.151,
                0.729,
                0.709,
                0.75
              ],
              "content": "Since Akash’s final answer was 24, we have the equation:"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_table_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.424,
            0.754,
            0.533,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": "4x - 4 = 24",
          "image_source": "images/page_14_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.424,
            0.777,
            0.552,
            0.797
          ],
          "content": "4(x - 1) = 24",
          "image_source": "images/page_14_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.423,
            0.801,
            0.757,
            0.823
          ],
          "content": "x – 1 = 6 (Dividing both sides by 4)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.826,
            0.523,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": "Thus, Akash thought of the number 7."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.855,
            0.846,
            0.895
          ],
          "content": "？ Can you think of a simple rule that you can use to get the starting number from the final answer?"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.933,
            0.193,
            0.95
          ],
          "content": "178"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
